The 'codegen' folder contains scripts that automatically generate TypeScript files from C# source definitions and constants, ensuring type safety and consistency between the C# backend and TypeScript frontend. These generation scripts run as an explicit `pnpm codegen` step (NOT part of the shipped `tsc` build, and never at runtime) to keep the checked-in TypeScript definitions up-to-date with the C# codebase. This approach eliminates manual synchronization efforts and reduces errors in maintaining equivalent data structures between the two codebases.
